From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nowon <nowon@noreply.pepecoin.surf>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:13:23 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 162/162] GreatDANE: N1 overlay hook, N2 idempotent apply,
 warn-once banner

N1: add greatdane/tools/apply-greatdane-overlay.sh as the in-repo
overlay apply hook; it execs apply-greatdane-static-prefs.sh (line 26).
The historical dane-linux pin sequences live outside this repo and
were not modified. They still need a call to the hook after product
git am and before mach configure.

N2: apply-greatdane-static-prefs.sh is idempotent and all-or-nothing.
Both patches are git apply --check'd before any write; already-applied
(git apply --reverse --check) is a no-op success; a partial pre-state
fails before writing; a failed second apply rolls the first back.
Tests cover a double run (no-op, no duplicates) and a partial
pre-state (nonzero, no writes).

Nits: log the ignored lazyAllowPreActivation override only once per
session; the about:dane banner uses the full pref name and tells the
user to reset it in about:config.

Local only, not pushed. No mach.
